<p><strong>Speculation on the Muon Optimizer</strong> (Response to Key Ques=
tion 2)</p>
<p>When discussing optimizers in the framework of stability analysis, these=
 arguments assume that gradients are bounded and the problem is convex. The=
 interaction between the learning rate and weight decay in Muon (or similar=
 momentum-based optimizers) may still exhibit a similar scaling pattern. Th=
is is because the gradient term captures the essence of Muon but is directl=
y constrained by existing upper bounds, whereas weight decay acts on the pa=
rameters, so its effect is <mjx-container class=3D"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attache=
