>Strengths And Weaknesses:</strong> <div class=3D"note-content-value markdo=
wn-rendered"><p>Strengths: </p>
<ol>
<li><p>This paper compared the generalization bounds for SGD and SGDM, with=
 and without weight decay based on stability, and demonstrated that weight =
decay improves  generalization and enforces stricter learning rate conditio=
ns for both SGD and SGDM.</p>
</li>
<li><p>This paper proposed a scaling rule for hyperparameters (including we=
ight decay coefficient), and this corroborates with the results in existing=
 work.</p>
</li>
<li><p>Experiments are conducted to verify the findings that weight decay e=
nhances generalization but also constrains the optimal learning rate. The p=
roposed hyperparameters scaling laws are validated across ResNet-18 for vis=
ion and Qwen3-0.6B for language modeling.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p>Weakness: </p>
<ol>
<li>Some existing works that are closely related to this paper are not cite=
d in this paper, for instance, the generalization analysis of SGD with weig=
ht decay.</li>
<li>The claims in this paper do not clearly specify the range to which they=
 apply. For example, Question 1 in fact goes beyond the results presented i=
n the paper. Also, this paper should include proper summaries that clearly =
state its actual contributions.</li>
<li>The clarity of this paper needs to be improved. For example, the abstra=
ct could be more concise and should clearly summarize the main idea of the =
paper, leaving more details for the main text. The main text could include =
some concise summaries and takeaways. Some minor typos are listed in the Qu=
estions section.</li>
</ol>
