<li><strong>Why match the generalization bounds of SWA and SGD-WD?</strong>=
</li>
</ul>
<p>In machine learning, weight decay is a typical explicit regularizer that=
 constrains parameters to achieve good generalization. SWA, a popular metho=
d, guides the model to flatter regions, which can be viewed as an implicit =
regularizer on the solution space. Under a simple convex objective, we use =
the same generalization capability as an equivalence to connect these two a=
lgorithms with different constraint behaviors.</p>
