<p><strong>W6-8</strong>  We ran 2 random seeds (42, 123) across three arch=
itectures (ResNet-18, VGG-16, ResNet-50), totaling ~640 runs. The half-rang=
e in stable regions is below 0.5%, confirming robustness. Adding VGG-16 and=
 ResNet-50 validated the stability boundary ordering, =CE=B7=E2=80=93=CE=BB=
 inverse relationship, and batch size scaling across architectures. Detaile=
d results are in the <a href=3D"https://anonymous.4open.science/r/wd_rebutt=
al-B375/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer">https://anonymous.4=
open.science/r/wd_rebuttal-B375/</a>.</p>
<p><strong>KQ1</strong> Figure 1 shows the optimal performance of SGD, SGD-=
WD, SGDM, and SGDM-WD. It demonstrates two points:</p>
<ul>
<li>Introducing <mjx-container class=3D"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0" jax=3D=
"CHTML" tabindex=3D"0" ctxtmenu_counter=3D"306" style=3D"font-size: 121.3%;=
 position: relative;"><mjx-math class=3D"MJX-TEX" aria-hidden=3D"true"><mjx=
